  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.26\n- Fixes the Uno Messaging registration so every head returns the builder. The Mac Catalyst branch previously fell through to the shared return outside the conditional block, which the compiler reported as unreachable code; each head now returns from its own branch.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.25\n- Fixes Mac Catalyst. The package now ships a net10.0-maccatalyst asset and delegates to Messaging.Apple on that head. Previously a net10.0-maccatalyst consumer resolved the plain net10.0 browser asset, so UseUno() threw UnoFirebaseMessagingException at startup.\n- Mac Catalyst defines MACCATALYST (and __IOS__), not IOS. The per-head dispatch is now IOS || MACCATALYST in both the using block and the registration branch; fixing only the asset or only the symbol leaves the failure in place.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Adds the Uno Platform integration for Firebase Messaging. UseUno() delegates to the platform package that matches the Uno head the application is running on.\n- The package references no Uno package and stays framework-independent, exactly as the .Maui packages reference no MAUI package. The head is detected at runtime, so the browser and Skia-desktop heads share the plain net10.0 asset.\n- Fails fast with UnoFirebaseMessagingException on the Windows head, because FireForNet ships no Windows Messaging implementation, and on the Skia desktop head, including Linux.",
